            <ArticleTitle>A variant neglected Type IIIA dorsal dislocation of first metatarsophalangeal joint. A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e27-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.fas.2014.11.009</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1268-7731(14)00154-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a rare injury consisting of a neglected, irreducible, dislocation of the first metatarsophalangeal joint that was diagnosed 4 months after the injury. An open reduction was necessary from the beginning. Patient returned to full activity without pain or disability, so a good prognosis despite the delayed diagnosis was achieved. We are unaware of previous reports in the literature describing this unusual variant.</AbstractText>
